{"id":"c-bill-wong--push-pull-legs-upper-lower-pplul","src":"coach","title":"Push Pull Legs Upper Lower (PPLUL)","author":"Dr. Swole","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/coaches/bill-wong/push-pull-legs-upper-lower-pplul","desc":"<p><strong>Program Structure</strong></p><p>Day 1 is Pull day instead of the traditional Push day. This is because we want to spread out back training from Leg day as much as possible, so your back is better recovered for squats.</p><p>Certain smaller muscle group accessories are mixed into other days to help you better target these muscles when you are fresher. For example, biceps are done at the end of Push instead of Pull day so you can hit them harder without back fatigue. Shoulder accessories like lateral raises are done at the end of Pull, Legs, and Lower days to help you train delts fresher and with more frequency.</p><p>The program starts off easy in week 1, but gradually increases in volume and RPE in week 2 and 3.</p><p>You can run this program indefinitely beyond 8 weeks.<br>For full details on PPLUL, please watch the YouTube overview linked below.</p>","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":13131,"rate":4.1384,"rateCount":1250,"updated":"2026-10-09T23:10:45.460Z","variations":[{"name":"Default","days":["Pull","Push","Legs","Upper","Lower"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Cable Row","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Upright Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raises","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":30,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Triset (little rest in between)"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"EZ Bar Skull Crusher","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"